WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.400
Spring 1942

3
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.200
Hitler's U-boats wreak havoc
in the North Atlantic

4
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:41.400
sinking over 1000 Allied ships
and threatening to destroy the supply line

5
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.200
from America to England. Unable to
crack the new U-boat radio codes.

6
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.200
the Allies struggle blindly
against the German onslaught.

7
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:28.400
Enemy speed eight.
Angle on the bow. sixty.

8
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.200
Mark is set.

9
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.100
Depth is set.

10
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.000
Range five hundred.

11
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:49.800
Set torpedo speed.
Thirty-five knots.

12
00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.500
Spread shots from tubes
one and four!

13
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.900
Tubes one and four ready.

14
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.900
Spread shots...

15
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:14.700
Fire!

16
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.800
Torpedoes running.

17
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.400
Great shot. Captain.

18
00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.000
We broke their back. Gentlemen.

19
00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.900
Fast screws! Bearing 180!

20
00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.000
A destroyer!

21
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:09.700
Down to ninety meters.
Both motors full ahead!

22
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.100
All hands forward!

23
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.500
Seal torpedo hatches!

24
00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.300
Starboard rudder twenty.

25
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.100
Rudder at twenty.

26
00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.800
Check all hull openings.

27
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.200
Come about.

28
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.100
Passing 200 degrees.

29
00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.300
Forty-five meters.
Fast dive. Captain.

30
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.000
Both hydroplanes. please.

31
00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.400
Steady at 220 degrees.

32
00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.000
Contact drawing right.

33
00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:14.900
Port engine stop.

34
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.500
Port engine has stopped.

35
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.100
Port engine half back.

36
00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.700
Depth charges!

37
00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:42.800
Hold on! The Tommies are
crapping all over us!

38
00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.100
Careful. that's fuel leaking!

39
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.200
Stop that leak!

40
00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.900
She's dropped to 120 meters. Captain.

41
00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.400
Blow all tanks! Surface! Surface!

42
00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.900
Everything clear.
Lookouts to the bridge!

43
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.500
Diesel room! Answer me!

44
00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.900
I need a damage report. Hans!

45
00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.800
They're all dead. Captain.
All our mechanics.

46
00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:35.700
The Chief Mechanic. the fat kid.
the whole engine crew. All dead.

47
00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:41.400
Port exhaust hatch broke.
Port diesel is flooded.

48
00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.600
Crankcase is full of seawater.
Starboard diesel...

49
00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.700
...seized two days ago.

50
00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:57.500
- What about my batteries?
- Damaged. 300 Amps bow. 200 stern.

51
00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.800
It's useless!

52
00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:07.900
We have only enough power to dive
and maybe maneuver around a bit.

53
00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:13.500
Thank you. Hans. Pass the word
to conserve electricity.

54
00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.300
- Radioman!
- Captain?

55
00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:23.700
To Berlin: Location 85-32.

56
00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:35.100
Both diesel engines out of service.
Electric motors only. Send help.

57
00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.500
There he is. Hey. Andy!

58
00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.600
Where you been?
It's an all-hands function.

59
00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.100
I want you to meet Joanie.
This is Andy Tyler.

60
00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.400
My best friend.
We went to Annapolis together.

61
00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.900
- Nice to meet you.
- I got you one of Larson's stogies.

62
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.400
- To our navy's next sub skipper.
- Thank you.

63
00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.200
Lieutenant! Gonna hoist up a few beers
with the enlisted boys later?

64
00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.800
- You got it. Griggs.
- All right.

65
00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.700
Mr. Tyler!

66
00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.900
My mom's visiting.
Do you want to meet her?

67
00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.400
Sure thing. Trigger.

68
00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.000
That's the lieutenant I was talking about.

69
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.500
Lieutenant Tyler!

70
00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:28.800
Hello there. Prudence. Louise.
Mrs. Dahlgren. Captain.

71
00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:32.200
Where's your date. Andy?
It's not like you to arrive stag.

72
00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:35.500
I'm afraid I couldn't get one
on such short notice. ma'am.

73
00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.700
Captain. could I have a word with you?

74
00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.600
Certainly. Darling. will you excuse us?

75
00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.300
Be right back.

76
00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.000
I didn't get my boat.

77
00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.200
I know.

78
00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.800
With all due respect. there's only
one way that could've happened...

79
00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.900
... and that's if you withheld
your recommendation.

80
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.800
That's right. I just don't think you're ready.

81
00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:13.100
What do you mean. I'm not ready?

82
00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.400
Sir. I have worked my tail off on the S-33.

83
00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.600
I'm qualified in every area and then some.

84
00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.100
No executive officer
has higher marks than I do.

85
00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.200
You're just not ready
to take on a command of your own.

86
00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:33.000
Now I've made my decision. It's done.

87
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.300
Mr. Tyler. How you doing. sir?

88
00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:45.200
- Having a good time?
- Hell yeah. Chief.

89
00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:49.500
- How about you?
- I'm looking forward to getting underway.

90
00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.100
I'm a sea dog. Need some salt. sir.

91
00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:58.100
He torpedoed me. Chief.

92
00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.500
Nine months aboard the S-33...

93
00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:04.800
... doing the best job I know how.

94
00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.800
Doing everything once
and then doing it again...

95
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:11.800
... just to make sure
I didn't miss anything the first time.

96
00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:16.200
You'll get your chance. sir.
There's other commands in the Navy.

97
00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:21.700
You knew?

98
00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.500
Didn't warn me.

99
00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.500
It ain't my place. sir.

100
00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.100
Club's secured! Time to go!

101
00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:41.000
Let's go. Get out. Everyone out.

102
00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.300
Come on. let's go.

103
00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.800
What's the meaning of this. Sergeant?

104
00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:49.200
- Are you the senior man?
- That's right. I'm the XO of the S-33.

105
00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.500
These men have a 48-hour liberty pass.

106
00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.500
No. sir. not no more.

107
00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:41.700
What the hell are those yard birds
doing to my boat?

108
00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.700
Looks like a goddamn Nazi submarine.

109
00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.800
Hey. Andy. This is a fine Navy day.

110
00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:56.700
They wouldn't give me five minutes to
consummate my marriage. Five minutes!

111
00:13:56.800 --> 00:14:00.000
- What's going on here?
- Hell if I know. Put your cover on.

112
00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.500
Yes. sir.

113
00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.100
- Mr. Tyler. call the crew to quarters.
- Aye. Captain.

114
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:09.300
Quarters! Everybody fall in!
Let's get in formation now!

115
00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.000
Let's go! Now! Formation!

116
00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.100
Prepare crew three.
Muster with first lieutenant.

117
00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.200
Prepare crew three.
Muster with first lieutenant.

118
00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:23.400
Captain. all crew members present
and accounted for. sir!

119
00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.300
Very well. At ease.

120
00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:31.700
I'm sorry your liberty's been cut short.
but our schedule's changed.

121
00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:36.500
We have two hours to get stowed
for sea and set the maneuvering watch.

122
00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:40.800
Sir Larson. have your torpedo men
load the tubes with their four best fish.

123
00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:44.400
Sir Emmett. warm up the diesels
and line up a battery charge.

124
00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.200
Sir Tyler. we have dry stores...

125
00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:49.400
... ordnance and perishables
to get below decks.

126
00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.100
Gentlemen. it's our turn.

127
00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.000
That's all.

128
00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.000
Attention!

129
00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.600
Aye. Captain.

130
00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:05.900
- Crew dismissed!
- You heard the man! Store his load!

131
00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:10.400
You got six seconds to get on your
boondockers and dungarees and turn to!

132
00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:14.200
- Is this for real. or is it a drill?
- "It's our turn. " what does that mean?

133
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.100
What about our liberty pass?
What's going on?

134
00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:22.200
I don't know. but I'm gonna find out.
Get your jobs done now.

135
00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.900
All off-going duty officers.
report to the dock...

136
00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:28.700
Captain Dahlgren. could you fill me in
on what's going on. sir?

137
00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.200
We're obviously not going
to the Caribbean station.

138
00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:34.100
No. we're not.
We're going on a special op.

139
00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.800
You'll be briefed with Mr. Emmett
and Mr. Larson once we get underway.

140
00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.000
- Aye. sir.
- Andy. listen.

141
00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:42.900
I'm gonna need the very best
from you on this run...

142
00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.900
... regardless of any differences
you may have with me.

143
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.900
Are we clear on that?

144
00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.300
- Yes. sir.
- Good.

145
00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:55.900
Now. go find Radioman Wentz and
quietly escort him to the materiel office.

146
00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.200
Mr. Tyler. How are you. son?

147
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.900
I'm fine. Admiral Duke.
What brings you up here?

148
00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:14.000
He does. That's Lieutenant Hirsch.
He's going to be riding your boat.

149
00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:18.600
You're not working for SubLant on this run.
Mr. Hirsch has operational control.

150
00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:21.800
He's the boss. Anything he wants. he gets.

151
00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:27.600
Fine.

152
00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.800
Is this him?

153
00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:41.000
I understand your family
comes from Koblentz.

154
00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:45.600
Good Rhine farming folk.

155
00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.500
You understand me. Mr. Wentz?

156
00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.000
Yes. sir.

157
00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:57.400
Can you speak passable German?
Can you read and write it?

158
00:16:57.900 --> 00:17:02.600
Or are you just a farm boy with
a German name?

159
00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:12.100
I am just a farm boy. One who can read.
write and speak quite well.

160
00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:20.300
I studied German at Brown University
before joining the war.

161
00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:29.000
Thank you. Wentz.

162
00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:33.400
- He'll do.
- Thank you. Wentz. That's all for now.

163
00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:35.800
Lieutenant. prepare the boat
to get underway.

164
00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.200
Aye. sir.

165
00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.700
Admiral.

166
00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:49.800
Mr. Tyler. please.
don't tell the other guys I'm half German.

167
00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:52.700
They'll hate me.

168
00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.300
Yeah. sure thing. Wentz.

169
00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:02.700
Prepare crew three.
Muster with first lieutenant.

170
00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:06.200
Prepare crew three.
Muster with first lieutenant.

171
00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:16.900
Duty Officer Lane to the paint shop.

172
00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:19.500
Duty officer to the paint shop.

173
00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.600
You all right. Mr. Tyler?

174
00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.900
Tiptop. Eddie. Tiptop.

175
00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.300
Wanna thank you for that liberty pass.

176
00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.300
My girl thanks you. too.

177
00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.900
You're a good man. Mr. Tyler.

178
00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:48.100
Heart's in the right place.

179
00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:51.000
Just need to give it some time.

180
00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.900
Yeah. I heard about what happened to you.

181
00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:03.800
That's one of the advantages
of bein' seen and not bein' seen.

182
00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:08.700
You'd be surprised some of the shit
we mess-doers hear.

183
00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:12.500
Boy. don't go droppin' my eggs.

184
00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:13.600
Damn.

185
00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:14.700
Excuse me. Mr. Tyler.

186
00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:19.300
Look. all you gotta do is pick 'em up
with both hands. boy. both hands!

187
00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:22.300
Tyler!

188
00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:26.500
When the hell were you gonna tell me?
I hear this from the chief.

189
00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:29.700
What do you want me to say?
He shit-canned me.

190
00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:32.000
Now you're gonna transfer to another boat.

191
00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.300
Excuse me.

192
00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.600
Either of you tell me where
I can find the exec?

193
00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:38.800
Yeah. that's me. Mac.
Move your truck. Unload here shortly.

194
00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.300
You'll unload it now. Here's the manifest.

195
00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:44.000
- Get those crates below decks.
- Who the hell are you?

196
00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:46.500
Marine Major Coonan.
Office of Naval Intelligence.

197
00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.600
I'm goin' to sea with you boys.

198
00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.400
That's my luggage.
You got a problem. talk to Mr. Hirsch.

199
00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:11.500
Clear!

200
00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.100
Cast off all lines forward!

201
00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:15.700
- Cast off forward!
- Take in all lines aft.

202
00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:17.300
Cast off aft!

203
00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.900
Rudder amidships. all ahead one-third.

204
00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.400
All ahead one-third!

205
00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.500
Bridge hatch shut.

206
00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:22.700
Engine room. secure the diesels.
Shift propulsion to the battery.

207
00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.300
Secure diesels.
shift propulsion to the battery.

208
00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:27.400
Main induction indicates shut.

209
00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:29.000
- Green board. skipper.
- Very well.

210
00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:32.000
Passing the 100-fathom curve.
On course. on time. sir.

211
00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:35.100
Engine room reports secured diesels.
propulsion switched.

212
00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:36.600
All ahead two-thirds.

213
00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.900
All ahead two-thirds.

214
00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:40.400
Mr. Emmett. take her down.

215
00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.300
Make her depth 150 feet.
10 degree down bubble.

216
00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:46.000
150 feet. 10 degree down bubble.

217
00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:49.500
Chief of the watch. sound the dive alarm.
Pass the word to 1MC.

218
00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:53.000
- Open the main ballast tank vents.
- Aye. sir. passing the word.

219
00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:56.700
Dive. dive. dive.

220
00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:00.400
Sir. main ballast tank vents indicate open.

221
00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:04.400
- Aye. Both planes dive 15 degrees.
- Both planes dive 15 degrees.

222
00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:07.800
All clear!

223
00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.900
- Decks awash.
- Decks awash. Aye. Sir.

224
00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:42.400
First time on a submarine?

225
00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:44.200
That's right.

226
00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.400
Sixty feet.

227
00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:53.700
Lower the scope.

228
00:22:56.400 --> 00:23:00.200
Captain. engine room reports minor
flooding from shaft seals and brine pump.

229
00:23:00.300 --> 00:23:03.400
- Bilge is at 18 inches and rising.
- Very well.

230
00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:07.200
How deep does this thing go?

231
00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:10.300
She'll go all the way to the bottom
if we don't stop her.

232
00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:12.900
Normally we try not to get below 150 feet.

233
00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:15.600
Any deeper.
the leaks overwhelm the pumps.

234
00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.800
These S-boats are antiques...

235
00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:20.300
... older than most of the crew.

236
00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:24.600
100 feet. Aye.

237
00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.900
Excuse me. Mr. Emmett.

238
00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:37.200
Put a pipe patch on it. lash it with marline.

239
00:23:37.300 --> 00:23:39.300
Yard can fix it when we get back to port.

240
00:23:39.400 --> 00:23:40.700
Yes. sir.

241
00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:46.200
Relax. gentlemen.
She's old. but she'll hold.

242
00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:51.700
Last night. at 0300 hours...

243
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:55.700
... a British destroyer reported depth
charging and sinking a German U-boat.

244
00:23:56.300 --> 00:23:58.000
However. some time thereafter...

245
00:23:58.100 --> 00:24:02.400
... Allied direction-finding stations
triangulated a coded enemy radio signal...

246
00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:05.700
... to this position here. near the chopline.

247
00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:08.900
We believe the U-boat was disabled.
not sunk...

248
00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:11.800
... and is drifting eastward
on a four-knot current.

249
00:24:12.100 --> 00:24:15.200
Now. French resistance reported
a resupply submarine...

250
00:24:15.400 --> 00:24:18.500
... sailed from the Lorient U-boat pens
yesterday afternoon...

251
00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:20.300
... with engine parts and mechanics.

252
00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:24.000
We believe it's gonna rendezvous
with the disabled U-boat.

253
00:24:25.300 --> 00:24:27.600
On board that U-boat is this.

254
00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:30.800
TOP SECRET

255
00:24:32.800 --> 00:24:35.500
- A typewriter?
- An Enigma code machine.

256
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:39.700
It allows the German navy to communicate
with its submarines in secret...

257
00:24:39.900 --> 00:24:43.800
... and our inability to decipher
their messages is costing us this war.

258
00:24:44.300 --> 00:24:45.700
Mr. Coonan?

259
00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:48.700
All right. this is basically
a Trojan horse operation.

260
00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:53.700
The S-33 will rendezvous with the U-boat.
posing as the German resupply sub.

261
00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:55.400
I'll lead a boarding party dressed...

262
00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:57.500
... in Kriegsmarine uniforms
to the enemy submarine.

263
00:24:57.600 --> 00:25:00.700
We will take it by force
and secure the Enigma.

264
00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:04.700
German survivors will be transferred
to the S-33. and the U-boat scuttled.

265
00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:07.500
The German resupply sub
will arrive at the rendezvous...

266
00:25:07.500 --> 00:25:10.900
... and will assume that the U-boat
succumbed to its wounds and sank.

267
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:13.500
The Germans must never suspect
we have the Enigma.

268
00:25:13.600 --> 00:25:16.000
- That is vital.
- So it's a race.

269
00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.900
- Yes. effectively.
- Who's the boarding party?

270
00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:21.000
Since you're the XO. you. sir.

271
00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:24.500
Mr. Emmett. Mr. Larson. Mr. Hirsch
and nine of your ship's company.

272
00:25:24.800 --> 00:25:27.600
The captain. of course.
will remain onboard the S-33.

273
00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:32.600
Mr. Coonan. our boys
are submarine sailors. not combat marines.

274
00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:35.300
The boys onboard that U-boat
are sailors. too.

275
00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:39.100
Your men will be ready. Lieutenant.
I'll train them myself.

276
00:25:40.100 --> 00:25:42.400
You've come to the right boat.

277
00:26:22.400 --> 00:26:25.600
Okay. Chief. Let's give it a test.

278
00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:43.900
You said you could repair engines?

279
00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:48.900
Captain. I apprenticed in my Uncle's
garage. fixing scooters.

280
00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:59.100
I need a mechanic!

281
00:27:06.600 --> 00:27:09.100
Ahoy! Friends!

282
00:27:09.800 --> 00:27:13.600
Stop! We have many wounded!

283
00:27:13.900 --> 00:27:15.500
Take us prisoner. please!

284
00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:17.800
What are they saying. Captain?

285
00:27:20.200 --> 00:27:21.300
Give us a hand!

286
00:27:21.400 --> 00:27:24.300
They desire to be our guests.

287
00:27:25.500 --> 00:27:28.100
Impossible. Shoot them.

288
00:27:31.500 --> 00:27:35.700
Standing orders of the F�hrer.
We will not pick up any survivors.

289
00:27:37.300 --> 00:27:43.600
If they are found. they will report
our position with much eagerness.

290
00:27:45.400 --> 00:27:47.400
Get on with it.

291
00:27:52.700 --> 00:27:54.500
Give us a hand!

292
00:27:54.800 --> 00:27:56.200
We have no...

293
00:28:23.500 --> 00:28:27.000
I'm telling you. she was hotter
than Dorothy Lamour and better built.

294
00:28:27.100 --> 00:28:28.300
- Really?
- Yeah.

295
00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:33.000
I could tell she was interested.
but she was classy. you know?

296
00:28:33.600 --> 00:28:37.000
The type of girl that wants you
to take her to a country club dance.

297
00:28:37.100 --> 00:28:39.700
Yeah. like you've ever been
inside a country club.

298
00:28:39.800 --> 00:28:42.300
Hey! Like I'd even want to. all right?

299
00:28:43.400 --> 00:28:47.400
Anyway. I can see
I'm not getting anywhere with her...

300
00:28:47.700 --> 00:28:50.700
... so what I do is. I use my secret weapon.

301
00:28:50.900 --> 00:28:54.000
I tell her about the S-26.
Does the trick right away.

302
00:28:54.100 --> 00:28:56.700
Don't be talking about that
while we're underway.

303
00:28:56.900 --> 00:29:00.500
- Why? What happened with the S-26?
- Yeah. what happened?

304
00:29:00.600 --> 00:29:02.900
- You guys don't know?
- No.

305
00:29:05.200 --> 00:29:07.700
She was running a test dive
down off Norfolk.

306
00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:11.200
Shaft seal failed.

307
00:29:11.800 --> 00:29:14.100
She sunk to 400 feet.

308
00:29:15.400 --> 00:29:18.700
Know how much water pressure
there is that deep?

309
00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:36.500
Mazzola. you will be the first one
eating powdered eggs on this cruise.

310
00:29:36.600 --> 00:29:38.500
Keep it up. you hear?

311
00:29:45.700 --> 00:29:47.000
Come in.

312
00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:56.800
This is our position. Captain.
We're still bucking some pretty heavy seas.

313
00:29:56.900 --> 00:29:59.600
I estimate us to be about three hours
behind schedule.

314
00:29:59.700 --> 00:30:02.800
I gave orders to run at flank speed
and hold off a trim dive...

315
00:30:02.900 --> 00:30:06.800
... until we make up the lost time.
- That's fine. Lieutenant.

316
00:30:08.600 --> 00:30:11.000
You're a first-rate XO. Andy.

317
00:30:11.600 --> 00:30:13.600
A damn good submariner.

318
00:30:16.400 --> 00:30:18.400
I know the men like you.

319
00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:21.300
I'd give my life for any one of them. sir.

320
00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.900
I know you would.
I'm not questioning your bravery.

321
00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.900
The question is: What about their lives?

322
00:30:30.700 --> 00:30:33.300
You and Mr. Emmett are good friends.

323
00:30:33.500 --> 00:30:36.000
You went to the academy together.

324
00:30:36.700 --> 00:30:39.700
Would you be willing to sacrifice his life?

325
00:30:39.800 --> 00:30:42.600
Or what about some
of the younger enlisted men?

326
00:30:42.700 --> 00:30:46.300
You know. a lot of those guys
look up to you like a big brother.

327
00:30:46.500 --> 00:30:49.500
You willing to lay their lives on the line?

328
00:30:51.800 --> 00:30:53.800
You see? You hesitate.

329
00:30:54.500 --> 00:30:57.200
But as a captain. you can't.

330
00:30:58.200 --> 00:30:59.900
You have to act.

331
00:31:00.300 --> 00:31:03.200
If you don't.
you put the entire crew at risk.

332
00:31:04.200 --> 00:31:07.400
Now that's the job. It's not a science.

333
00:31:07.900 --> 00:31:12.600
You have to be able to make hard
decisions. based on imperfect information.

334
00:31:12.800 --> 00:31:16.600
Asking men to carry out orders
that may result in their deaths.

335
00:31:16.700 --> 00:31:21.400
And if you're wrong.
you suffer the consequences.

336
00:31:22.500 --> 00:31:25.700
If you're not prepared
to make those decisions...

337
00:31:25.800 --> 00:31:29.500
... without pause. without reflection...

338
00:31:31.100 --> 00:31:34.300
... then you've got no business
being a submarine captain.

339
00:31:39.800 --> 00:31:43.300
Tell Mr. Hirsch
I'd like a word with him. would you?

340
00:31:46.300 --> 00:31:47.600
Aye. sir.

341
00:32:51.800 --> 00:32:54.200
- More soup. Captain?
- Thank you.

342
00:32:55.700 --> 00:32:58.400
I wish I was going with you. gentlemen.

343
00:32:58.500 --> 00:33:01.100
I feel the same way you do. Carson.

344
00:33:01.600 --> 00:33:04.300
Gentlemen. I'd like to propose a toast.

345
00:33:04.500 --> 00:33:06.900
To the officers and crew of the S-33...

346
00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:10.300
... and our distinguished guests.
Mr. Hirsch and Mr. Coonan.

347
00:33:11.400 --> 00:33:13.700
- Success. gentlemen!
- Success.

348
00:33:17.400 --> 00:33:19.800
- Captain Dahlgren. sir?
- What is it. Wentz?

349
00:33:19.900 --> 00:33:23.300
Chief says we've picked up
a radar contact at 070�.

350
00:33:23.800 --> 00:33:26.400
Very well. Mr. Larson?

351
00:33:43.100 --> 00:33:45.600
Signal lamp off the starboard bow!

352
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:50.300
I see it.

353
00:33:52.700 --> 00:33:56.400
Pass the word along:
Submarine sighted off the starboard bow.

354
00:33:56.500 --> 00:33:58.600
- Stand by to man battle stations.
- Aye. sir.

355
00:34:01.200 --> 00:34:04.000
All right. here we go. One last time.

356
00:34:04.200 --> 00:34:08.500
Lt. Tyler's raft gets from the conning tower
aft. My raft gets the gun crew.

357
00:34:08.600 --> 00:34:11.200
And no one. no one shoots till I shoot first.

358
00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:13.400
- You read me?
- Yes. sir.

359
00:34:14.100 --> 00:34:16.400
Outstanding. Lock and load.

360
00:34:26.200 --> 00:34:28.300
It'll be all right. son.

361
00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:36.900
Captain. I estimate the German resupply
sub has a 14-knot speed of advance.

362
00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:39.300
My latest plot puts them
at 12 hours away. sir.

363
00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:40.600
Very well. Mr. Larson.

364
00:34:40.600 --> 00:34:44.100
Captain. the boarding party's ready. sir.
Await your go-ahead.

365
00:34:44.300 --> 00:34:45.500
I put her low in the water.

366
00:34:45.600 --> 00:34:49.300
I wanna give that U-boat
as little silhouette as we can.

367
00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:52.800
- Sir?
- Prepare to disembark the boarding party.

368
00:34:52.900 --> 00:34:54.400
Aye. Captain.

369
00:34:57.800 --> 00:34:59.900
If this thing goes south...

370
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.500
... I will blow that Nazi boat
right out of the water.

371
00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:05.500
- Understood. sir.
- Very well.

372
00:35:34.700 --> 00:35:36.400
All set. Captain.

373
00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:38.600
Now you listen to me.

374
00:35:38.700 --> 00:35:41.600
You get them their damn trophy
and get the hell out of there.

375
00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:45.100
- Aye. sir.
- The boys are gonna be fine.

376
00:35:46.900 --> 00:35:48.800
I know they will. sir.

377
00:35:52.100 --> 00:35:53.300
Good luck. Andy.

378
00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:57.100
Godspeed. skipper.

379
00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:32.500
Our comrades have brought us fresh
eggs. bananas and even our mail.

380
00:37:32.300 --> 00:37:35.500
Easy. Mr. Hirsch. We're almost there.

381
00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:38.900
We'll bushwhack them real good.

382
00:37:44.300 --> 00:37:47.700
All right. we got 12 men topside.
three on the bridge...

383
00:37:48.300 --> 00:37:50.600
... four on the foredeck. five aft.

384
00:37:51.800 --> 00:37:55.900
Now remember: Both rafts need
to be tied up before we move.

385
00:38:00.300 --> 00:38:02.600
Jesus H. Christ. They got machine guns.

386
00:38:03.800 --> 00:38:05.200
Steady. gentlemen.

387
00:38:06.300 --> 00:38:08.100
Wait for the signal.

388
00:38:13.400 --> 00:38:16.100
Ahoy!

389
00:38:22.200 --> 00:38:23.600
Mr. Hirsch.

390
00:38:27.200 --> 00:38:30.000
Ahoy! Welcome.

391
00:38:30.300 --> 00:38:33.600
Have we got a job for you.

392
00:38:34.900 --> 00:38:36.300
Mr. Hirsch.

393
00:38:38.900 --> 00:38:41.600
- Hello the boat. you asshole.
- Shut up.

394
00:38:52.000 --> 00:38:53.900
Goddamn you. Hirsch. say something.

395
00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:58.400
Which of you are the mechanics?

396
00:39:08.900 --> 00:39:11.900
We're all mechanics.
And we're all very skilled.

397
00:39:12.600 --> 00:39:16.100
We'll have you underway before dawn.

398
00:39:16.900 --> 00:39:18.600
Ahoy!

399
00:39:19.500 --> 00:39:21.200
Who wants this junk?

400
00:39:22.200 --> 00:39:29.000
Pornography and dirty letters
stinking of French perfume.

401
00:39:29.700 --> 00:39:32.400
A sack of pure shit.

402
00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:35.300
I should throw it overboard.

403
00:39:57.400 --> 00:39:58.900
Welcome aboard.

404
00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:21.200
- Let's go!
- Board this thing! Get out of the rafts!

405
00:40:21.400 --> 00:40:24.200
Repel Boarders! Alarm dive!

406
00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:26.600
Conning tower! Move. move!

407
00:40:30.200 --> 00:40:32.400
Clear the conning tower now!

408
00:40:36.900 --> 00:40:39.200
Another one there!

409
00:40:39.700 --> 00:40:41.900
- Griggs is hit!
- Get him off!

410
00:40:47.300 --> 00:40:50.400
- Move. move!
- Trigger. on the back!

411
00:40:53.100 --> 00:40:54.400
Griggs!

412
00:40:54.900 --> 00:40:56.800
We gotta get inside!

413
00:40:58.000 --> 00:40:59.700
Chief. Tank. come down now!

414
00:41:01.800 --> 00:41:03.100
Ready?

415
00:41:04.800 --> 00:41:07.600
Quick. open it! Fire!

416
00:41:09.900 --> 00:41:11.600
Tyler. let's go!

417
00:41:11.700 --> 00:41:13.300
Inside!

418
00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:16.000
Cover your men! Go. go!

419
00:41:21.900 --> 00:41:24.400
Don't let 'em close it.
Don't let 'em close it!

420
00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:32.500
Flood all the tanks!

421
00:41:32.600 --> 00:41:36.000
Let's drown these vermin!
Move your asses!

422
00:41:36.400 --> 00:41:40.500
Faster! Take her down. down!

423
00:41:46.200 --> 00:41:48.600
Two. three. four. five. Shut it.

424
00:41:50.700 --> 00:41:52.800
Let's go. Go! Get down! Go!

425
00:41:52.900 --> 00:41:54.500
Go. go!

426
00:42:04.800 --> 00:42:05.700
Get off him!

427
00:42:05.800 --> 00:42:08.900
Don't move. Get back. get back!

428
00:42:09.500 --> 00:42:11.500
Just drop it. Drop it!

429
00:42:21.100 --> 00:42:22.600
Get 'em out of here.

430
00:42:23.100 --> 00:42:25.600
- Did they hit you?
- I'm okay. sir.

431
00:42:30.900 --> 00:42:33.500
Stern team. go! Bow team. go!

432
00:42:39.200 --> 00:42:41.300
I'm out of clips. sir. You go ahead.

433
00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:45.200
- Rabbit!
- All right. get 'em out of here.

434
00:42:45.300 --> 00:42:47.400
Get 'em out of here! Let's go!

435
00:42:47.500 --> 00:42:49.400
Get down! Down. down!

436
00:42:49.600 --> 00:42:51.200
All right. who's the captain?

437
00:42:51.800 --> 00:42:53.900
Who's the captain? Kapit�n?

438
00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:56.100
How about you. ugly? You the captain?

439
00:42:56.200 --> 00:42:59.900
Trigger. if anybody moves. you shoot 'em
right in the forehead. understand?

440
00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.600
- Yes. sir!
- All right.

441
00:43:20.800 --> 00:43:22.200
Hirsch. we got it.

442
00:44:29.500 --> 00:44:33.300
- Down there!
- Down!

443
00:44:33.800 --> 00:44:37.200
Rabbit. check the bilge for a scuttling
charge. Give me your weapon!

444
00:44:37.300 --> 00:44:39.600
- Move. sailor. move!
- Aye. sir!

445
00:44:42.500 --> 00:44:44.400
Goddamn it. stay there.

446
00:44:47.100 --> 00:44:51.100
- Hirsch. I think we got the codebooks!
- That ink's running. Dry it.

447
00:44:52.900 --> 00:44:56.800
It's water soluble.
Yeah. use the blankets. use the blankets.

448
00:44:59.300 --> 00:45:01.300
Nothing but pipes and valves. Mr. Emmett.

449
00:45:01.700 --> 00:45:03.800
Bow compartment secure.

450
00:45:27.900 --> 00:45:29.400
Bunch of Marys.

451
00:45:32.600 --> 00:45:36.200
How you doing?
You're number 10. There you go.

452
00:45:37.600 --> 00:45:39.700
You having a good night?

453
00:45:40.800 --> 00:45:43.300
You ain't gonna be none
too happy you lost this boat.

454
00:45:43.400 --> 00:45:45.700
Lucky number 11. let's go!

455
00:45:47.200 --> 00:45:50.100
It's your first time
looking at a black man. ain't it?

456
00:45:50.200 --> 00:45:51.800
Get used to it.

457
00:45:52.300 --> 00:45:54.400
Let's go! Get over here!

458
00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:32.400
All right. hurry it up.
It's gonna be sunup in an hour.

459
00:47:11.500 --> 00:47:14.100
- Fuse is burning. sir.
- All right. she's burning!

460
00:47:14.200 --> 00:47:15.700
Let's get this raft loaded!

461
00:47:16.400 --> 00:47:17.800
Let's move!

462
00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:22.000
Sir. we got all the prisoners
transferred to the S-33.

463
00:47:22.100 --> 00:47:23.500
Very well.

464
00:47:31.300 --> 00:47:32.600
Hey. Andy.

465
00:47:33.300 --> 00:47:36.000
Make sure you got everything!
Get it in the raft!

466
00:47:36.100 --> 00:47:38.800
Get everything below decks. Let's go!

467
00:48:20.500 --> 00:48:23.000
Everybody. below decks! Get down!

468
00:48:23.200 --> 00:48:25.000
- Chief. take her down!
- Aye. sir!

469
00:48:25.100 --> 00:48:27.400
- Let's go. Hirsch!
- The Enigma!

470
00:48:32.700 --> 00:48:34.100
Trigger!

471
00:48:34.800 --> 00:48:35.900
Grab hold!

472
00:48:40.000 --> 00:48:41.700
Trigger!

473
00:48:41.800 --> 00:48:43.300
Attaboy!

474
00:48:48.000 --> 00:48:49.300
Got it!

475
00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:52.800
Help me! No!

476
00:49:00.700 --> 00:49:04.500
- We gotta get out of here!
- There's still men in the water.

477
00:49:04.600 --> 00:49:06.800
- Let's go!
- There's still men in the water.

478
00:49:06.900 --> 00:49:08.000
Go!

479
00:49:15.100 --> 00:49:16.600
Andy!

480
00:49:18.900 --> 00:49:20.800
Go!

481
00:49:22.300 --> 00:49:23.400
Dive!

482
00:49:24.800 --> 00:49:25.800
Dive!

483
00:49:27.600 --> 00:49:29.900
Take her down!

484
00:49:32.800 --> 00:49:33.900
Dive!

485
00:49:43.800 --> 00:49:45.500
Tyler. let's go!

486
00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:39.200
- Chief. you find those vents?
- Everything's in German!

487
00:50:39.300 --> 00:50:41.000
Rabbit. get to the torpedo room.

488
00:50:41.100 --> 00:50:43.500
Where's the goddamn 1MC?
Trigger. get on the helm!

489
00:50:43.600 --> 00:50:45.700
- Mazzola. take the planes!
- Aye. sir.

490
00:50:46.000 --> 00:50:48.100
- Wentz. what about these?
- I don't know.

491
00:50:48.200 --> 00:50:52.200
There's no label!
Okay. those are the aft ballast tanks vents!

492
00:50:52.300 --> 00:50:55.800
These are the midship vents.
and these are the main induction valves.

493
00:50:55.900 --> 00:50:57.200
Make sure they're shut.

494
00:50:57.300 --> 00:50:58.900
Tank. I need speed!

495
00:50:59.000 --> 00:51:00.500
Get the screws turning.

496
00:51:00.600 --> 00:51:03.300
The lights are on.
so there's got to be some power left.

497
00:51:03.400 --> 00:51:04.200
I can't read this!

498
00:51:04.300 --> 00:51:07.100
Find out how many fish are
in the tubes and figure out...

499
00:51:07.200 --> 00:51:08.500
... how to launch 'em! Go!

500
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:10.600
I can't read this!

501
00:51:10.700 --> 00:51:12.600
Go help Tank. Hirsch. Go. Hirsch!

502
00:51:14.000 --> 00:51:15.300
Find the Christmas tree.

503
00:51:16.100 --> 00:51:18.500
We've gotta make sure
there's no holes in the boat!

504
00:51:18.600 --> 00:51:21.200
"Klar. " Wentz. what the hell is "klar"?

505
00:51:21.600 --> 00:51:24.400
"Klar" means "clear."
All compartments secure.

506
00:51:24.500 --> 00:51:28.900
White for green? No holes in the ship!
Dive the boat. Chief!

507
00:51:29.100 --> 00:51:32.200
- Opening ballast vents!
- Opening midship valves!

508
00:51:32.600 --> 00:51:34.200
Opening midship vents!

509
00:51:43.600 --> 00:51:47.400
This is forward trim. aft trim.
These are auxiliaries.

510
00:51:47.900 --> 00:51:50.400
Main motor. Auxiliary. auxiliary.

511
00:52:06.000 --> 00:52:09.400
This is in meters. Everything's in meters.
Passing 15 meters.

512
00:52:09.900 --> 00:52:11.400
Recommend shutting main vents!

513
00:52:11.500 --> 00:52:14.600
Make it so! Get in the sound room.
Let me know what's out there.

514
00:52:14.700 --> 00:52:15.600
Yes. sir!

515
00:52:15.800 --> 00:52:17.900
- Take depth 20 meters.
- Depth 20 meters. aye.

516
00:52:18.000 --> 00:52:21.600
- Chief. take the dive!
- I have the dive.

517
00:52:22.100 --> 00:52:26.100
At 20 meters. Bow planes at zero.
Control your depth with the stern planes.

518
00:52:26.200 --> 00:52:28.900
Bow planes at zero.
Controlling depth with stern planes.

519
00:52:29.400 --> 00:52:31.800
Oh. shit. All ahead full. sir!

520
00:52:32.100 --> 00:52:34.300
Batteries are flat and draining fast!

521
00:52:34.500 --> 00:52:37.800
Mr. Tyler. I hear the S-33 breaking up.
Wait.

522
00:52:38.500 --> 00:52:41.700
I hold a submerged U-boat. 010�.

523
00:52:41.800 --> 00:52:44.000
Real close. Less than 1.000 yards.

524
00:52:44.100 --> 00:52:46.300
Goddamn resupply sub.
What's our heading?

525
00:52:46.400 --> 00:52:47.500
280�. sir!

526
00:52:47.500 --> 00:52:50.400
All right. right full rudder! Steady on 010�!

527
00:52:50.500 --> 00:52:53.600
Aye. sir! Right full rudder.
Steady on course 010�.

528
00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:56.400
Tank. starboard back full.
Rabbit. get back to me.

529
00:52:56.500 --> 00:52:58.900
Starboard back full. Aye. sir.

530
00:53:04.200 --> 00:53:07.100
- Watch your depth. She'll squat.
- Rabbit!

531
00:53:08.800 --> 00:53:10.600
We got four fish. Tubes are flooded.

532
00:53:10.800 --> 00:53:13.000
But I can't open the doors
until I'm equalized.

533
00:53:13.100 --> 00:53:15.300
- I can't find the valve!
- Wentz. help Rabbit!

534
00:53:15.400 --> 00:53:16.900
Enemy submarine close aboard.

535
00:53:17.000 --> 00:53:19.300
Torpedo in the water.
Torpedo in the water!

536
00:53:19.400 --> 00:53:21.200
Belay that. Wentz. stay where you are!

537
00:53:21.300 --> 00:53:23.300
Hirsch. hotfoot it to the torpedo room!

538
00:53:26.400 --> 00:53:28.800
- Helm. mark a head every 10 degrees.
- Aye. sir.

539
00:53:29.000 --> 00:53:32.600
- Now passing 320�.
- Turn. baby. turn. Turn!

540
00:53:35.200 --> 00:53:38.000
Equalizing valves. Holy shit!
What's what? This is crazy!

541
00:53:38.100 --> 00:53:39.900
I can't equalize the tubes!

542
00:53:40.800 --> 00:53:42.600
- What do you need?
- Equalizing valves!

543
00:53:42.700 --> 00:53:44.200
Equalizing valves!

544
00:53:44.300 --> 00:53:45.600
- Gyro!
- No.

545
00:53:45.800 --> 00:53:47.700
- Drainage!
- No!

546
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:50.400
Now passing 000�.

547
00:53:50.900 --> 00:53:53.000
Swing. you bastard. swing.

548
00:53:54.400 --> 00:53:58.000
Chief. stand by in case
we have to flood forward trim.

549
00:54:02.200 --> 00:54:03.400
- Impulse?
- No.

550
00:54:03.400 --> 00:54:06.200
- Differential! Pressure differential!
- Turn 'em. yes.

551
00:54:06.300 --> 00:54:08.600
- Which way?
- Counterclockwise.

552
00:54:17.700 --> 00:54:19.600
Torpedo missed. It's in our baffles.

553
00:54:22.800 --> 00:54:25.200
Two more torpedoes in the water!

554
00:54:25.300 --> 00:54:29.000
Best bearing to the U-boat: 010�.

555
00:54:29.100 --> 00:54:31.300
Rabbit. get ready to fire a spread.

556
00:54:31.500 --> 00:54:34.700
Tubes one and two. Zero gyro. Fire!

557
00:54:34.900 --> 00:54:36.500
Rabbit. fire!

558
00:54:40.300 --> 00:54:41.300
What's going on?

559
00:54:41.400 --> 00:54:44.400
- What is that?
- Wrong one! The fish is stuck!

560
00:54:44.500 --> 00:54:48.900
- We missed an interlock.
- Get those fish out before they blow!

561
00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:53.700
- Look for "impulse air" or "firing air."
- That one's "impulse" there!

562
00:54:58.000 --> 00:55:01.000
One. two. away.
Lining up tubes three and four.

563
00:55:01.400 --> 00:55:02.900
Three and four. fire!

564
00:55:10.500 --> 00:55:13.500
All fish running hot. straight and normal.

565
00:55:42.300 --> 00:55:44.600
I think they all missed. sir.

566
00:55:57.700 --> 00:55:59.000
Shit.

567
00:56:04.200 --> 00:56:06.100
U-boat's breaking up!

568
00:56:07.400 --> 00:56:09.100
I hear bulkheads collapsing.

569
00:56:13.900 --> 00:56:15.700
The 33 boat. Mr. Tyler.

570
00:56:23.100 --> 00:56:25.400
Let's take her up and look
for survivors. Chief.

571
00:56:25.500 --> 00:56:27.800
- Give me some rise on the planes!
- Rise on the planes.

572
00:56:27.900 --> 00:56:29.700
Deploy main ballast!

573
00:57:14.600 --> 00:57:16.200
Oh. crap.

574
00:57:23.900 --> 00:57:25.000
Help!

575
00:57:26.900 --> 00:57:28.100
Help!

576
00:57:29.400 --> 00:57:31.600
Please! Help!

577
00:57:32.100 --> 00:57:34.500
Help!

578
00:58:10.100 --> 00:58:11.900
Do you speak English?

579
00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:15.400
English. Do you speak English?

580
00:58:16.200 --> 00:58:18.100
What's your rank?

581
00:58:19.100 --> 00:58:20.800
What do you do?

582
00:58:21.400 --> 00:58:23.500
What's your job? Your job.

583
00:58:23.700 --> 00:58:24.900
"Job."

584
00:58:32.700 --> 00:58:35.000
You're an electrician. Good.

585
00:58:35.200 --> 00:58:39.000
You can help us squeeze more juice
out of them batteries.

586
00:58:40.700 --> 00:58:42.700
Sir. I see the skipper.

587
00:58:57.100 --> 00:58:58.700
Battery's dead.

588
00:58:59.100 --> 00:59:01.800
Whatever juice was left we used up
when we maneuvered.

589
00:59:01.900 --> 00:59:03.300
What about the diesels?

590
00:59:03.400 --> 00:59:06.600
Starboard's a wreck.
We need the dry dock to fix it.

591
00:59:07.100 --> 00:59:08.700
Portside diesel's the good news.

592
00:59:08.800 --> 00:59:11.500
Whoever the Krauts had on it
didn't know a piston head...

593
00:59:11.600 --> 00:59:12.800
... from his sister's titty.

594
00:59:13.100 --> 00:59:14.600
I think I can fix it.

595
00:59:14.700 --> 00:59:16.800
Okay. Tank.

596
00:59:17.100 --> 00:59:20.200
- Do what you can.
- Yes. sir.

597
00:59:21.400 --> 00:59:23.300
All right. Listen up.

598
00:59:24.000 --> 00:59:26.200
We've decided on a course.

599
00:59:27.000 --> 00:59:29.300
We're headin' for England. Land's End.

600
00:59:29.400 --> 00:59:32.400
It's the closest. besides occupied France.

601
00:59:33.700 --> 00:59:36.000
Rabbit. how many torpedoes do we have?

602
00:59:36.100 --> 00:59:41.000
Just one. It's in the stern tube. which is
busted. bleedin' air from somewhere.

603
00:59:41.100 --> 00:59:43.500
- Sir?
- Yeah. what is it. Trigger?

604
00:59:43.700 --> 00:59:46.000
Can't we just use the radio?

605
00:59:46.100 --> 00:59:48.100
Fire off a mayday and wait for a rescue?

606
00:59:48.900 --> 00:59:50.300
That's impossible.

607
00:59:50.400 --> 00:59:53.800
If we transmit. the Germans will
direction-find our position to a grid...

608
00:59:53.900 --> 00:59:55.900
... with their missing two U-boats.

609
00:59:55.900 --> 01:00:00.000
If they even suspect we have the Enigma.
they'll change their entire coding system.

610
01:00:00.100 --> 01:00:03.100
And that would completely negate
the purpose of our mission.

611
01:00:03.200 --> 01:00:04.600
Mr. Tyler...

612
01:00:05.200 --> 01:00:07.000
... if we head for England...

613
01:00:07.000 --> 01:00:10.100
... we're gonna go straight
through the western approaches.

614
01:00:10.300 --> 01:00:13.700
He's right. I mean. that's Jerry's backyard.

615
01:00:14.300 --> 01:00:16.400
- Listen. guys...
- It's full of U-boats.

616
01:00:16.500 --> 01:00:18.800
And we've got nothing
to defend ourselves with.

617
01:00:18.800 --> 01:00:21.600
Do you think I got all the answers here?

618
01:00:21.600 --> 01:00:24.300
Think I know how we're gonna
get out of this? I don't.

619
01:00:24.400 --> 01:00:26.600
I don't know how.

620
01:00:26.600 --> 01:00:29.200
- I say we use the radio.
- Nobody asked you.

621
01:00:29.300 --> 01:00:32.600
- We use the radio and take our chances.
- I said can it.

622
01:00:32.600 --> 01:00:36.200
- It's what the captain would have done...
- Captain's dead.

623
01:01:55.100 --> 01:01:56.700
This is crazy.

624
01:01:57.800 --> 01:02:00.000
This whole thing is crazy.

625
01:02:00.200 --> 01:02:02.600
Riskin' our lives over a typewriter.

626
01:02:02.700 --> 01:02:05.400
- It's not a typewriter.
- The hell it ain't.

627
01:02:05.500 --> 01:02:07.700
- It's got buttons like a typewriter.
- It's not.

628
01:02:07.800 --> 01:02:11.300
Whatever it is.
it's crazy we get killed over it.

629
01:02:11.700 --> 01:02:14.700
The Navy says it's important.
it's important.

630
01:02:15.200 --> 01:02:18.000
The Navy says it's more important
than you. him. me. fine.

631
01:02:18.100 --> 01:02:20.100
We're gonna die trying.

632
01:02:21.000 --> 01:02:23.900
And that ain't crazy. That's our job.

633
01:02:25.700 --> 01:02:29.800
What I don't understand. Chief.
is how come you're not in charge?

634
01:02:29.900 --> 01:02:33.900
Scuttlebutt is Dahlgren was kicking Tyler
out of the Navy anyway. and...

635
01:02:35.200 --> 01:02:37.500
You stow that shit right now. sailor.

636
01:02:38.100 --> 01:02:42.500
Lt. Tyler is your commanding officer.
and you will respect that man as such.

637
01:02:43.500 --> 01:02:45.900
- Do you understand?
- Yes. Chief.

638
01:03:33.700 --> 01:03:36.000
Look at them sons of bitches.

639
01:03:37.600 --> 01:03:40.000
You know my pop was a fisherman?

640
01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:44.900
He had this old 60-footer
he'd run all over the gulf.

641
01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:47.000
Noisy two-stroke diesel.

642
01:03:48.400 --> 01:03:50.800
Rotten to the gunnels. that thing.

643
01:03:50.900 --> 01:03:55.300
I could scrub that deck three times a day.
and it still stunk like fish.

644
01:03:56.600 --> 01:03:59.900
And I swore I'd never skipper
a boat like that. Chief.

645
01:04:03.600 --> 01:04:08.000
I saw myself standing on the bridge
of a battleship.

646
01:04:09.500 --> 01:04:11.500
A real sea captain.

647
01:04:12.600 --> 01:04:15.200
Mr. Tyler. permission to speak freely?

648
01:04:15.900 --> 01:04:17.600
Of course. Chief.

649
01:04:18.400 --> 01:04:20.200
This is the Navy...

650
01:04:20.800 --> 01:04:24.700
... where a commanding officer
is a mighty and terrible thing.

651
01:04:24.800 --> 01:04:27.000
A man to be feared and respected.

652
01:04:27.100 --> 01:04:29.700
All knowing. all powerful.

653
01:04:29.800 --> 01:04:32.900
Don't you dare say what you said
to the boys back there again...

654
01:04:33.000 --> 01:04:34.100
... "I don't know."

655
01:04:34.200 --> 01:04:38.100
Those three words will kill a crew
dead as a depth charge.

656
01:04:39.300 --> 01:04:41.200
You're the skipper now...

657
01:04:41.300 --> 01:04:45.600
... and the skipper always knows
what to do. whether he does or not.

658
01:04:49.600 --> 01:04:52.100
- Aircraft off the port bow!
- Shit!

659
01:05:02.800 --> 01:05:06.000
Real sorry. sir.
It dropped right out of the clouds.

660
01:05:06.100 --> 01:05:08.200
Rabbit. Trigger. stand by the flak gun.

661
01:05:08.300 --> 01:05:09.700
Sir.

662
01:05:10.500 --> 01:05:14.100
It's German.
Looks like long-range reconnaissance.

663
01:05:15.300 --> 01:05:17.700
What the hell's it doing way out here?

664
01:05:23.200 --> 01:05:25.900
- Jesus. here it comes.
- All right. Sit tight.

665
01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:29.800
As far as he knows. we're all playing
on the same team. Everybody wave.

666
01:05:30.400 --> 01:05:31.600
Wave?

667
01:05:32.400 --> 01:05:35.300
Sir. we're sitting ducks.
We could blow 'em out of the sky.

668
01:05:35.600 --> 01:05:37.900
We miss. he's gonna radio us in.

669
01:05:38.100 --> 01:05:40.400
That plane's gonna be
the least of our problems.

670
01:05:40.800 --> 01:05:43.800
This is crazy. You're gonna get us killed.

671
01:05:52.300 --> 01:05:55.200
He's coming around. He's coming around.

672
01:06:00.800 --> 01:06:02.500
He's attacking! Rabbit. do something!

673
01:06:02.600 --> 01:06:04.300
Shut up. Rabbit. ignore him.

674
01:06:04.400 --> 01:06:05.400
Do something!

675
01:06:05.500 --> 01:06:08.600
He's coming at us!
He's coming right at us! Do something!

676
01:06:08.700 --> 01:06:11.100
- Acknowledge me. Parker!
- What are you waiting for?

677
01:06:11.200 --> 01:06:13.300
- Shoot him!
- Parker. I'm ordering you!

678
01:06:13.400 --> 01:06:16.200
Do not fire that weapon!
Get your finger off that trigger!

679
01:06:16.300 --> 01:06:18.500
Pull the trigger! Pull the trigger!

680
01:06:18.600 --> 01:06:20.800
We're gonna die! Do it!

681
01:06:20.900 --> 01:06:23.800
Come on! Goddamn it. can't you see him?

682
01:06:31.700 --> 01:06:33.200
What the hell are you doing?

683
01:06:33.300 --> 01:06:35.700
This is not a goddamn democracy!

684
01:06:37.900 --> 01:06:40.700
Mr. Tyler. I see a mast on the horizon!

685
01:06:45.000 --> 01:06:47.400
Shit! That's a Nazi destroyer.

686
01:06:48.600 --> 01:06:52.100
That plane must have been runnin'
a recon screen for it.

687
01:06:53.000 --> 01:06:56.100
Clear the bridge!
Chief. secure the diesel and dive the ship!

688
01:06:56.200 --> 01:06:58.300
Dive the ship! Aye. sir!

689
01:07:54.900 --> 01:07:57.800
We don't have a green board.
The engine room's not ready.

690
01:07:57.800 --> 01:08:00.800
Vents won't open. we lost hydraulics.

691
01:08:00.900 --> 01:08:04.600
Tank. secure the diesel
and rig the engine room for dive!

692
01:08:05.600 --> 01:08:07.400
Tank. acknowledge!

693
01:08:08.300 --> 01:08:12.500
Goddamn it! Mazzola.
go see what the hell's going on back there.

694
01:09:21.300 --> 01:09:24.000
Drop it. you Nazi son of a bitch! Drop it!

695
01:09:33.400 --> 01:09:34.800
Goddamn it.

696
01:09:36.800 --> 01:09:39.000
I'm real sorry. Mr. Tyler.

697
01:09:39.400 --> 01:09:41.600
Took me right off my feet.

698
01:09:42.100 --> 01:09:44.800
Listen to me.
You've got to secure the diesel.

699
01:09:44.900 --> 01:09:47.500
And find out why the vent valves
won't open. Now!

700
01:09:48.100 --> 01:09:49.700
- Yes. sir.
- Goddamn it!

701
01:09:49.800 --> 01:09:53.300
Eddie. get this son of a bitch out of here.
Chain him to the bunks.

702
01:09:53.400 --> 01:09:57.100
Make sure his hands and feet are secure.
Put him into submission!

703
01:09:57.200 --> 01:10:00.800
- Lieutenant. we have a problem!
- Take care of it. Eddie.

704
01:10:09.200 --> 01:10:10.500
Oh. shit.

705
01:10:18.800 --> 01:10:22.300
Tell Tank to finish those repairs.
The destroyer is sending a launch.

706
01:10:22.400 --> 01:10:24.300
He needs five minutes. Mr. Tyler!

707
01:10:24.500 --> 01:10:26.800
We don't have five minutes. Chief.

708
01:10:26.900 --> 01:10:30.600
Lieutenant. the deck cannon.
if we fire a shell below the water line...

709
01:10:30.700 --> 01:10:32.600
It wouldn't do a goddamn thing.

710
01:10:32.700 --> 01:10:35.100
No. that tub could take 100 shells.

711
01:10:35.200 --> 01:10:38.200
What we need is a working torpedo.
which we do not have.

712
01:10:38.300 --> 01:10:39.900
Trigger. stand by on the flak gun.

713
01:10:40.000 --> 01:10:42.200
On my order.
turn that launch into driftwood.

714
01:10:42.300 --> 01:10:43.600
Yes. sir.

715
01:10:44.000 --> 01:10:47.100
Gonna find out who we are
in about 60 seconds.

716
01:10:51.400 --> 01:10:53.300
Trigger. ready on that weapon?

717
01:10:53.400 --> 01:10:55.300
Chief. tell Tank he has one minute...

718
01:10:55.400 --> 01:10:59.200
... and get Wentz and Rabbit up here
with the machine gun.

719
01:10:59.700 --> 01:11:02.300
What happens when
they find out we're not German?

720
01:11:02.400 --> 01:11:05.800
After they shoot us as spies.
they'll radio into headquarters.

721
01:11:06.000 --> 01:11:08.500
They'll tell them
the Enigma's been compromised.

722
01:11:10.100 --> 01:11:14.000
What if we take out their radio.
before they can notify anyone about us?

723
01:11:14.100 --> 01:11:17.100
- How?
- With that deck gun.

724
01:11:17.900 --> 01:11:20.400
It's gonna be one hell of a shot.
but we can do it.

725
01:11:20.700 --> 01:11:23.800
Then we dive like hell.
and we get under them quick.

726
01:11:24.000 --> 01:11:28.100
We lure 'em a little bit closer to the
continent. in range of Allied air cover.

727
01:11:28.300 --> 01:11:32.200
- Then we call in an air strike.
- Yeah. we call in an air strike.

728
01:11:34.000 --> 01:11:36.600
Son of a bitch cut off pressure
to the hydraulics.

729
01:11:36.700 --> 01:11:39.500
Let's find the stop valve.

730
01:11:44.800 --> 01:11:45.800
Damn!

731
01:11:49.300 --> 01:11:52.800
See that structure topside
with the big antenna sticking out of it?

732
01:11:52.900 --> 01:11:54.500
- Yes. sir.
- That's the radio shack.

733
01:11:54.600 --> 01:11:56.000
You. Wentz. get on the deck gun.

734
01:11:56.100 --> 01:11:59.600
On my command.
put a shell right through the porthole.

735
01:12:01.600 --> 01:12:05.200
- Get to it. gentlemen. Get to it.
- Yes. sir!

736
01:12:10.500 --> 01:12:15.100
Hello. Gentlemen.
Give us a hand with the lines.

737
01:12:18.400 --> 01:12:19.800
What are they doing?

738
01:12:22.700 --> 01:12:23.900
Something's wrong.

739
01:12:24.400 --> 01:12:26.900
Tell them to go away. Mr. Hirsch.

740
01:12:34.300 --> 01:12:36.200
Back to the ship!

741
01:12:38.200 --> 01:12:39.300
Talk to me. Rabbit!

742
01:12:39.600 --> 01:12:41.700
Deck gun manned and ready
in all respects. sir!

743
01:12:42.100 --> 01:12:43.700
Fire!

744
01:13:00.100 --> 01:13:01.700
Clear the deck!

745
01:13:08.900 --> 01:13:11.200
Get to the forward gun!
They're firing on us!

746
01:13:11.500 --> 01:13:12.400
Who. sir?

747
01:13:12.600 --> 01:13:15.300
The submarine.
They've blown up our radio tower!

748
01:13:20.200 --> 01:13:21.400
- All right.
- Come on!

749
01:13:27.600 --> 01:13:30.700
Dive! Dive!

750
01:13:44.200 --> 01:13:45.700
Come on. Why aren't we diving?

751
01:13:45.700 --> 01:13:47.700
Repairs aren't complete. sir.

752
01:13:47.800 --> 01:13:49.100
Eddie. man the planes.

753
01:13:49.200 --> 01:13:51.000
- Tank. all ahead full.
- Aye. sir!

754
01:13:50.900 --> 01:13:51.700
Manning planes!

755
01:13:51.800 --> 01:13:53.600
All ahead full. aye!

756
01:13:54.100 --> 01:13:57.500
Nice shot. Rabbit. That radio is history.

757
01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:05.500
Come on.

758
01:14:07.200 --> 01:14:10.000
- We're heading right towards them.
- That's right.

759
01:14:10.600 --> 01:14:13.500
Their deck guns can't get to us
if we're in close enough.

760
01:14:13.600 --> 01:14:16.600
Let's hope we can dive and clear her keel.

761
01:14:30.200 --> 01:14:31.900
That's it.

762
01:14:32.300 --> 01:14:33.800
Hydraulics restored!

763
01:14:33.900 --> 01:14:37.200
Thank you. Tank.
That did it. We're going under.

764
01:14:47.200 --> 01:14:49.000
Passing five meters.

765
01:14:58.600 --> 01:15:00.300
Passing ten meters.

766
01:15:06.900 --> 01:15:08.500
Fifteen meters.

767
01:15:37.300 --> 01:15:38.900
Twenty meters.

768
01:16:14.600 --> 01:16:16.700
Trigger. left full rudder.

769
01:16:20.500 --> 01:16:22.500
Tank. all ahead two-thirds.

770
01:16:32.300 --> 01:16:33.700
Contact maneuvering.

771
01:16:37.500 --> 01:16:39.200
Heavy cavitation.

772
01:16:41.300 --> 01:16:44.000
- Splashes.
- Shit.

773
01:16:52.400 --> 01:16:54.500
Short intervals.

774
01:16:56.400 --> 01:17:01.100
Prepare charges.
Set depth twenty-five.

775
01:17:57.300 --> 01:18:01.000
Step away from that bulkhead. Mr. Hirsch.

776
01:18:02.000 --> 01:18:06.100
The shock wave from one of these
explosions can snap your spine.

777
01:18:10.500 --> 01:18:11.800
Chief...

778
01:18:13.100 --> 01:18:15.500
... you ever been depth charged?

779
01:18:15.600 --> 01:18:18.800
Once. off Murmansk...

780
01:18:18.800 --> 01:18:21.100
... back in World War I.

781
01:18:21.700 --> 01:18:26.300
One charge came so close. it rattled
four teeth out of the skipper's head.

782
01:18:37.400 --> 01:18:39.100
Wasn't even close.

783
01:18:46.500 --> 01:18:49.300
Control. starboard e-motor's seized up.

784
01:18:50.200 --> 01:18:53.900
- The German must have sabotaged it.
- Goddamn it.

785
01:18:57.400 --> 01:19:02.100
There's no way we make it to Allied
air cover creeping along on one shaft.

786
01:20:58.000 --> 01:21:00.600
Eddie. help Chief.

787
01:21:02.700 --> 01:21:04.200
Yes. sir.

788
01:21:11.700 --> 01:21:13.600
Mr. Chief. I got that.

789
01:21:15.900 --> 01:21:19.400
Tank. you alive back there?

790
01:21:21.200 --> 01:21:22.500
Yes. sir.

791
01:21:22.700 --> 01:21:27.700
Good. Port ahead two-thirds.

792
01:21:28.900 --> 01:21:31.400
Port ahead two-thirds. Aye. sir.

793
01:21:57.500 --> 01:21:59.400
Tank...

794
01:21:59.700 --> 01:22:01.400
... can you fix the stern tube?

795
01:22:03.200 --> 01:22:04.900
I don't know. Mr. Tyler.

796
01:22:05.500 --> 01:22:07.900
I don't want an "I don't know."

797
01:22:08.700 --> 01:22:12.700
Can you fix the torpedo tube? Yes or no?

798
01:22:15.300 --> 01:22:17.300
Yes. sir. I think I can.

799
01:22:18.300 --> 01:22:19.600
Thank you. Tank.

800
01:22:19.700 --> 01:22:23.500
Chief. make depth 160 meters.

801
01:22:27.600 --> 01:22:29.600
That's more than 500 feet.

802
01:22:32.400 --> 01:22:34.100
Take us down. Chief.

803
01:22:37.100 --> 01:22:38.400
Aye. sir.

804
01:22:39.500 --> 01:22:41.400
160 meters.

805
01:22:41.600 --> 01:22:43.500
Twenty degrees dive. both planes.

806
01:22:43.500 --> 01:22:45.100
Twenty degrees dive. aye. sir.

807
01:22:46.400 --> 01:22:48.100
Mr. Tyler. sir...

808
01:22:49.400 --> 01:22:51.900
... do you plan on going up
against a destroyer...

809
01:22:52.000 --> 01:22:55.200
... with only one fish in the tube
and a busted motor?

810
01:22:55.700 --> 01:22:57.400
Yes. I am. Eddie.

811
01:22:57.600 --> 01:23:00.500
- How wise is that. Lieutenant?
- Not very.

812
01:23:01.000 --> 01:23:03.000
But have a look. Chief.

813
01:23:04.500 --> 01:23:07.000
There is no way a 2-knot submarine...

814
01:23:07.000 --> 01:23:12.100
... can get in firing position against
a 30-knot destroyer unless we go deep.

815
01:23:12.600 --> 01:23:14.000
At 160 meters...

816
01:23:14.100 --> 01:23:17.000
... we can shoot out some junk
from the forward tubes.

817
01:23:17.100 --> 01:23:19.700
It will resurface and create a debris field.

818
01:23:19.800 --> 01:23:22.700
The destroyer will go to the center
of that debris field...

819
01:23:22.800 --> 01:23:25.100
... shut off its engines to be quiet...

820
01:23:25.200 --> 01:23:27.900
... and do an acoustic search
to make sure we're dead.

821
01:23:28.000 --> 01:23:31.000
But we're not. See. we're here...

822
01:23:31.100 --> 01:23:34.000
... on our way up to periscope depth.

823
01:23:34.400 --> 01:23:36.500
All right. principle of ascent velocity.

824
01:23:36.600 --> 01:23:40.100
Our positive buoyancy pulls us up
and away from the destroyer.

825
01:23:40.200 --> 01:23:43.400
And when we surface.
we'll be showing it our ass at 700 yards.

826
01:23:43.800 --> 01:23:48.000
That is a perfect setup for a stern shot
on a stationary target.

827
01:23:48.200 --> 01:23:51.900
Boom. It don't get much prettier than that.

828
01:23:54.300 --> 01:23:56.100
All right. Mr. Tyler.

829
01:23:57.600 --> 01:23:59.500
Passing 130 meters.

830
01:23:59.600 --> 01:24:00.800
Very well.

831
01:24:01.100 --> 01:24:05.100
Rabbit. I need you to load Mazzola's body
into tube three...

832
01:24:05.200 --> 01:24:09.100
... and put an escape jacket
on him to make sure he floats.

833
01:24:09.800 --> 01:24:12.300
Want to shoot him out like garbage?

834
01:24:19.400 --> 01:24:21.900
His body is gonna save our lives.

835
01:24:23.600 --> 01:24:25.500
I'll say a few words for him.

836
01:24:25.600 --> 01:24:29.200
Hirsch. go with Rabbit.
Eddie. can you man both planes?

837
01:24:29.200 --> 01:24:30.400
Yes. sir.

838
01:24:30.800 --> 01:24:32.500
- Tyler.
- Yeah.

839
01:24:32.700 --> 01:24:35.100
If you can't take out that destroyer...

840
01:24:35.200 --> 01:24:37.700
... the danger is not
that some of us may die.

841
01:24:38.100 --> 01:24:40.500
It's that some of us may live.

842
01:24:43.000 --> 01:24:46.000
These men have seen and heard things...

843
01:24:46.300 --> 01:24:49.100
... that must not be revealed to the enemy.

844
01:24:49.200 --> 01:24:50.900
Our secrets...

845
01:24:51.600 --> 01:24:53.600
... such as our radar capabilities...

846
01:24:53.600 --> 01:24:56.800
... and our understanding
of German encryption.

847
01:24:58.400 --> 01:25:02.700
If we fall into German hands alive.
we will be tortured without mercy.

848
01:25:02.800 --> 01:25:05.700
Either you succeed in sinking that ship...

849
01:25:06.000 --> 01:25:09.500
... or you must see to it
that none of us survive...

850
01:25:09.900 --> 01:25:11.600
... to be captured.

851
01:25:44.100 --> 01:25:46.300
We commend his soul to God...

852
01:25:47.400 --> 01:25:50.000
... and commit his body to the deep.

853
01:25:57.300 --> 01:26:00.200
Mr. Tyler. contact is zigging.

854
01:26:04.100 --> 01:26:05.600
Splashes.

855
01:26:07.300 --> 01:26:09.300
Contact getting closer.

856
01:26:10.400 --> 01:26:11.900
More splashes.

857
01:26:23.200 --> 01:26:27.800
Tank. line up to pump
engine room bilge to sea.

858
01:26:28.300 --> 01:26:29.600
Yes. sir.

859
01:26:44.300 --> 01:26:45.700
Rabbit...

860
01:26:47.700 --> 01:26:49.200
... fire the tubes.

861
01:26:51.500 --> 01:26:53.000
'Bye. Mazzola.

862
01:28:08.500 --> 01:28:11.400
They're setting the charges too shallow.

863
01:29:31.300 --> 01:29:33.200
Secure that air valve!

864
01:29:47.600 --> 01:29:50.500
Chief. what's our depth?

865
01:29:52.000 --> 01:29:53.800
160 meters.

866
01:29:56.000 --> 01:29:58.900
Zero the planes.

867
01:29:59.100 --> 01:30:00.500
Splashes!

868
01:30:03.200 --> 01:30:05.300
They're too close together!

869
01:30:06.000 --> 01:30:07.800
I can't count them.

870
01:30:17.100 --> 01:30:18.400
Chief...

871
01:30:20.500 --> 01:30:22.300
... take us to 200 meters.

872
01:30:24.900 --> 01:30:27.700
We're gonna get under these damn things.

873
01:30:31.000 --> 01:30:32.200
Chief...

874
01:30:33.000 --> 01:30:35.500
... take us to 200 meters.

875
01:30:42.400 --> 01:30:43.700
Aye. sir.

876
01:30:49.900 --> 01:30:52.400
Making my depth 200 meters.

877
01:30:53.000 --> 01:30:55.000
Ten degrees dive. both planes.

878
01:30:55.100 --> 01:30:57.000
Ten degrees dive. Aye.

879
01:31:20.700 --> 01:31:22.600
170 meters.

880
01:31:35.400 --> 01:31:36.600
Tank...

881
01:31:37.100 --> 01:31:40.100
... what's the status
on the stern torpedo tube?

882
01:31:41.300 --> 01:31:44.900
There's a couple things wrong.
I can operate the muzzle door...

883
01:31:45.100 --> 01:31:47.300
... but I'm still working on the impulse air.

884
01:31:47.400 --> 01:31:49.300
180 meters.

885
01:31:51.800 --> 01:31:55.100
Mr. Tyler. depth gauge back here
says 180 meters.

886
01:31:56.000 --> 01:31:58.300
Thanks. Tank. I know.

887
01:32:00.100 --> 01:32:01.600
Keep working.

888
01:32:14.000 --> 01:32:15.900
190 meters.

889
01:32:36.700 --> 01:32:39.000
200 meters.

890
01:32:39.800 --> 01:32:43.200
- Zero the planes.
- Zero the planes. aye.

891
01:33:46.500 --> 01:33:48.700
Mary. mother of God.

892
01:33:53.600 --> 01:33:57.100
Those Krauts
sure know how to build a boat.

893
01:34:05.100 --> 01:34:06.800
Chief. take us up!

894
01:34:06.900 --> 01:34:10.600
- Slowing negative! Planes full rise!
- Clockwise. Hirsch!

895
01:34:13.600 --> 01:34:16.800
- Rabbit. help me out!
- Go! Go!

896
01:34:20.100 --> 01:34:22.200
Chief. are you seeing this?

897
01:34:29.000 --> 01:34:33.300
Needle's off the scale!
We have to blow main ballast tanks!

898
01:34:33.400 --> 01:34:34.900
Do it. Chief!

899
01:34:52.600 --> 01:34:56.900
- She's still going down!
- Ballast tanks are bone dry!

900
01:34:57.000 --> 01:34:59.100
I'm gonna try the trim tanks!

901
01:35:05.500 --> 01:35:07.200
Come on. come on!

902
01:35:19.100 --> 01:35:21.500
She's going up! She's going up!

903
01:35:37.900 --> 01:35:40.100
Mr. Tyler. we're coming up.

904
01:35:40.700 --> 01:35:43.100
But I've lost control of the ballast tanks.

905
01:35:43.200 --> 01:35:45.300
I can't stop our ascent.

906
01:35:46.400 --> 01:35:48.200
Where are we with the stern torpedo?

907
01:35:48.200 --> 01:35:49.600
Piping's damaged.

908
01:35:49.800 --> 01:35:53.700
There's a break in the air line.
so there's no pressure to launch a torpedo.

909
01:35:53.800 --> 01:35:57.400
I tried to bypass the leak.
but it's way back in the bilge underwater.

910
01:35:57.500 --> 01:36:00.300
There's no way to reach it. I can't fit.

911
01:36:00.400 --> 01:36:03.100
- Can somebody else get to it?
- I don't know.

912
01:36:04.200 --> 01:36:06.200
Maybe somebody smaller.

913
01:36:07.000 --> 01:36:08.800
That's Rabbit or Trigger.

914
01:36:09.000 --> 01:36:11.100
Coming up on 200 meters.

915
01:36:12.000 --> 01:36:13.800
You gotta pick one.

916
01:36:21.500 --> 01:36:22.800
Trigger.

917
01:36:23.100 --> 01:36:26.500
Trigger. lay aft with Tank.

918
01:36:28.500 --> 01:36:33.100
Move it. son. You got a job to do.

919
01:36:41.300 --> 01:36:44.400
See. we got no air pressure
to fire the torpedo.

920
01:36:44.600 --> 01:36:46.800
One of these pipes is busted
and leaking air.

921
01:36:46.900 --> 01:36:50.400
- How am I gonna find it?
- You'll see bubbles coming out. Lot of 'em.

922
01:36:50.600 --> 01:36:54.900
Find the isolation valve aft of the leak
and crank it down.

923
01:36:55.000 --> 01:36:56.800
- Got it?
- Yeah.

924
01:36:58.300 --> 01:37:00.700
I rigged this hose
so you can breathe through it.

925
01:37:00.900 --> 01:37:04.300
Now listen to me.
As soon as you finish. you get out of there.

926
01:37:04.600 --> 01:37:06.600
- Okay?
- Yeah.

927
01:37:27.500 --> 01:37:29.100
I can hear her.

928
01:37:31.000 --> 01:37:32.800
Making slow turns.

929
01:37:38.100 --> 01:37:40.200
She just stopped her screws.

930
01:37:43.300 --> 01:37:45.600
I think they see the debris.

931
01:37:48.700 --> 01:37:50.300
I think they're buying it.

932
01:37:50.600 --> 01:37:52.700
180 meters.

933
01:37:54.100 --> 01:37:57.400
Chief. can you slow our ascent?
We are not ready.

934
01:37:58.200 --> 01:37:59.600
Can't. sir.

935
01:38:00.500 --> 01:38:02.900
We got a one-way ticket topside.

936
01:38:05.200 --> 01:38:08.900
If we surface without
a torpedo to fire. we're dead.

937
01:38:47.300 --> 01:38:48.600
There are two air leaks.

938
01:38:48.700 --> 01:38:50.700
I got one. but the other's too far back.

939
01:38:50.800 --> 01:38:52.800
I need some more slack
on the hose to reach.

940
01:38:53.000 --> 01:38:55.100
- That's all there is.
- Shit.

941
01:39:16.800 --> 01:39:19.400
150 meters.

942
01:39:23.200 --> 01:39:25.300
I hear Morse code.

943
01:39:26.100 --> 01:39:29.500
What the hell is it? Are they signaling us?

944
01:39:37.400 --> 01:39:39.400
What's it saying. Wentz?

945
01:39:39.400 --> 01:39:41.900
"I am U-571. Destroy me."

946
01:39:53.500 --> 01:39:55.800
Coming up on 90 meters.

947
01:40:13.000 --> 01:40:16.100
Sir. she's started her engines again.

948
01:40:20.000 --> 01:40:22.900
No go. Mr. Tyler. He can't reach.

949
01:40:31.000 --> 01:40:35.100
Trigger. in one minute we're gonna hit
the surface. Do you understand me?

950
01:40:35.200 --> 01:40:37.700
Now you've got
to go back in there and try.

951
01:40:37.900 --> 01:40:40.200
I wouldn't ask if our lives
didn't depend on it.

952
01:40:40.300 --> 01:40:42.600
- Sorry. sir. Can't reach it.
- No. Trigger.

953
01:40:42.700 --> 01:40:44.400
Now listen to me.

954
01:40:45.700 --> 01:40:48.500
You can reach it. and you will.

955
01:40:49.100 --> 01:40:52.800
- Now you are gonna close that valve.
- I can't!

956
01:40:52.900 --> 01:40:55.300
You're the only chance we've got.

957
01:40:59.400 --> 01:41:02.200
Now you're gonna go back down
in that bilge...

958
01:41:02.400 --> 01:41:05.400
... and you're gonna do your job. sailor.

959
01:41:17.600 --> 01:41:20.200
Report to me the instant
that torpedo's ready to fire.

960
01:41:20.300 --> 01:41:21.600
Yes. sir.

961
01:41:24.200 --> 01:41:25.800
Thirty meters.

962
01:41:26.300 --> 01:41:28.600
- Talk to me. Wentz.
- Destroyer is underway.

963
01:41:28.600 --> 01:41:31.700
Steady bearing.
They're closing our position.

964
01:41:32.100 --> 01:41:35.100
Shit! Come on. Trigger!

965
01:41:36.000 --> 01:41:37.000
Twenty meters.

966
01:41:37.700 --> 01:41:39.600
Hold on. We're gonna surface.

967
01:41:39.700 --> 01:41:41.300
Raising scope.

968
01:41:51.000 --> 01:41:52.300
Got her.

969
01:41:53.200 --> 01:41:55.300
She's heading right for us.

970
01:41:55.600 --> 01:41:58.400
- Helm. come right 10 degrees.
- Aye. sir!

971
01:41:58.500 --> 01:42:01.300
- Watch your bow planes.
- Aye. sir. Watching my bow planes.

972
01:42:01.400 --> 01:42:04.300
Tank. start the diesel. All ahead full!

973
01:42:12.700 --> 01:42:14.700
Port diesel ahead full!

974
01:42:36.100 --> 01:42:37.900
Shit. they've got us bracketed.

975
01:42:39.700 --> 01:42:41.000
Incoming!

976
01:42:48.300 --> 01:42:49.800
We're hit!

977
01:42:50.800 --> 01:42:54.000
- Wentz. get in here!
- Eddie. secure that hatch!

978
01:43:12.700 --> 01:43:14.600
Tube still not ready!

979
01:43:21.400 --> 01:43:24.900
- Request permission to abandon ship!
- Not yet. Chief.

980
01:43:46.500 --> 01:43:49.700
Control. aft torpedo ready in all respects!

981
01:43:49.800 --> 01:43:50.900
Hold us here.

982
01:43:51.000 --> 01:43:54.300
- Hold us steady right here.
- Steady on bearing 80 degrees!

983
01:43:55.700 --> 01:43:57.100
Fire!

984
01:43:58.400 --> 01:44:00.900
Tank. fire right now or we die!

985
01:44:06.600 --> 01:44:08.900
Come on. come on.

986
01:44:12.600 --> 01:44:13.900
Torpedo!

987
01:45:08.900 --> 01:45:11.400
That blew them right in half.

988
01:45:22.600 --> 01:45:26.100
Hell. Mr. Tyler. if you ever need a chief...

989
01:45:26.600 --> 01:45:28.600
... I'd go to sea with you anytime.

990
01:45:30.400 --> 01:45:32.100
Thank you. Chief.

991
01:45:42.200 --> 01:45:43.700
Tank. you okay?

992
01:45:46.900 --> 01:45:48.600
Trigger drowned.

993
01:45:59.000 --> 01:46:01.400
That kid didn't give up. did he?

994
01:46:05.300 --> 01:46:07.400
Neither did you. Mr. Tyler.

995
01:46:18.900 --> 01:46:22.600
We can't keep her afloat much longer. sir.

